    "reasoning": "The earlier selected answers agree with every captured final solution. No grade evidence is supplied. Two source defects remain: q-105261 incorrectly labels a row scaling as -1/2 instead of +1/2, although its final answer is correct; q-127043 offers two mathematically valid radio choices, options 1 and 2, which are opposite direction vectors. Its worked solution explicitly supports option 1. Independently: q-105261 has u=-b-2c, so s=-1, t=-2 and st=2. In q-34142 and q-105291, the selected vectors equal -3a1 and a1/3 respectively. In q-34276, a3=a1-a2 proves dependence, so only III is true. In q-105315, the determinant is -6, proving independence and making II and III true. In q-36023 and q-127002, constant coordinates give the base point and coefficients of t give the direction vector. Those coefficients also give the parallel vectors for q-32785 and q-127043. In q-32817, the image shows P=(-1,3,2) and Q=(2,4,5), so Q-P=(3,1,3). In q-127065, adding t times the supplied direction to the supplied point gives the parametric equations. In q-127078 and q-70866, setting each symmetric ratio equal to t gives the parametric equations. In q-71028 and q-127405, eliminating t gives the symmetric equations. In q-71035, the zero x direction component requires x=-3 separately, with (y-6)/10=(z+2)/3. All selected values reproduce the source answers; none of the final source answers is mathematically wrong.",
